CAT = "cpabarPublic"; SEG = "PUB"
Q = [
("Rule 3-01 of Regulation S-X requires a registrant to file audited consolidated balance sheets as of the end of its most recent:",
 "Two fiscal years", ["Three fiscal years", "One fiscal year", "Five fiscal years"],
 "Rule 3-01(a) calls for audited balance sheets at the end of each of the two most recent fiscal years. Income and cash flow statements cover three years."),
("Rule 3-02 of Regulation S-X requires audited statements of comprehensive income and cash flows for each of the:",
 "Three most recent fiscal years", ["Two most recent fiscal years", "Five most recent fiscal years", "Last four quarters"],
 "Rule 3-02(a) requires three fiscal years, or a shorter period if the registrant has existed for less time. An emerging growth company may file less in an IPO."),
("Under Item 105 of Regulation S-K, if the risk factor discussion runs longer than 15 pages, the registrant must include:",
 "A summary of two pages or less", ["An auditor's review of the risks", "A ranking of each risk", "A ten-year risk history"],
 "Item 105(b) requires a series of concise bullet or numbered statements, no more than two pages, summarizing the principal risk factors."),
("The main purpose of XBRL in SEC filings is to:",
 "Make financial data machine-readable", ["Replace the auditor's report", "Encrypt the filed statements", "Shorten the filing deadlines"],
 "XBRL tags each amount and disclosure with a standard element so the data can be searched, compared and analyzed by software."),
("Segment revenues, external plus intersegment, are A $420M, B $160M, C $95M, D $85M and E $40M. Under the 10% revenue test, how many segments are reportable?",
 "4 segments", ["2 segments", "3 segments", "5 segments"],
 "Combined revenue is $800M, so the threshold is $80M. Segments A, B, C and D meet it, and E at $40M does not, so 4 segments are reportable.",
 sum(1 for r in (420, 160, 95, 85, 40) if r >= 0.10 * (420 + 160 + 95 + 85 + 40))),
("Under ASU 2023-07, a public entity must disclose, for each reportable segment, the significant expenses that are:",
 "Regularly provided to the CODM", ["Above 10% of segment revenue", "Paid in cash during the year", "Allocated from headquarters"],
 "ASU 2023-07 requires significant segment expenses that are regularly provided to the chief operating decision maker and included in the reported measure of segment profit or loss."),
("Which statement or information is required for a defined benefit pension plan but not for a defined contribution plan?",
 "Accumulated plan benefits", ["Net assets for benefits", "Changes in net assets", "Investments at fair value"],
 "A defined benefit plan reports the actuarial present value of accumulated plan benefits and changes in it. Both plan types present net assets available for benefits and changes in them."),
("A defined contribution plan begins the year with net assets of $12,000,000. Employer contributions are $1,100,000, participant contributions $700,000, investment income $900,000, benefits paid $1,300,000 and administrative expenses $50,000. Year-end net assets available for benefits are:",
 "$13,350,000", ["$14,650,000", "$13,400,000", "$11,950,000"],
 "Net assets are $12,000,000 + $1,100,000 + $700,000 + $900,000 - $1,300,000 - $50,000 = $13,350,000. Leaving out benefits paid gives $14,650,000.",
 12000000 + 1100000 + 700000 + 900000 - 1300000 - 50000),
]
